input.findings:
## Root cause (verified)

`src/scale/Log.ts:67` rounds every tick's un-logged value with `numberUtil.round` at its *default* precision:

```
src/scale/Log.ts:65-68
        return zrUtil.map(ticks, function (tick) {
            const val = tick.value;
            let powVal = fixRound(mathPow(base, val));
            let roundingCriterion = null;
```

`fixRound` is `numberUtil.round` (`src/scale/Log.ts:34`), and `round` is `toFixed`-based with default precision 10, clamped to `ROUND_SUPPORTED_PRECISION_MAX = 20`:

```
src/util/number.ts:158-167
export function round(x: number | string, precision?: number, returnStr?: boolean): string | number {
    if (precision == null) {
        precision = 10;
    }
    // Avoid range error
    precision = Math.min(Math.max(0, precision), ROUND_SUPPORTED_PRECISION_MAX);
    // PENDING: 1.005.toFixed(2) is '1.00' rather than '1.01'
    x = (+x).toFixed(precision);
    return (returnStr ? x : +x);
}
```

So `round(1e-15)` === `+(1e-15).toFixed(10)` === `0`. Every log tick whose value is below 1e-10 collapses to `0` (verified in node: `10^-15/-19/-50/-69` all → `0`, while `10^-10` and larger survive). Result: a log axis over e.g. `[2.9e-69, 1.6e-59]` returns ticks `[0, 0, 0, ...]`, the axis/series render garbage. Even bumping the precision does not help — `toFixed` maxes out at 20 fractional digits, so anything below 1e-20 is unrecoverable (`(1e-40).toFixed(20) === '0.00000000000000000000'`).

The rounding is not merely under-powered, it is **unnecessary**. `LogScale.calcNiceTicks` (src/scale/Log.ts:140-168) forces `interval` to an integer (`while (... Math.abs(interval) < 1 ...) interval *= 10;`) and the nice extent to integer multiples of it, and `base` is an integer (default 10). `Math.pow(intBase, intExp)` is exactly the IEEE-754 double nearest the decimal literal — verified: for exponents -69, -50, -19, -15, -10, -9, -3, 0, 3, 15, 23, `Math.pow(10, e) === Number('1e'+e)` is `true` in every case. There is no float error to "fix" here, so the rounding-error fix must simply be dropped. (This matches upstream apache/echarts commit `da1c932` / PR #21120, whose entire `src/` diff is this one statement; the reviewer rationale is in the PR #21107 review comment r2217334774.)

## Change 1 — REQUIRED: `src/scale/Log.ts` (`getTicks`)

Exact current text (src/scale/Log.ts:65-71):

```ts
